change:
  id: CHG-006
  title: Typed fitness signal identifiers
  status: delivered
  intent: Replace role-bearing fitness name prefixes with typed, canonical identifiers while preserving scoring behavior and providing a compatibility path for existing result keys.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - CON-002
    - ARCH-001
    - Q-004

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: Fitness signals use `subject.invariant.<name>`, `subject.objective.<name>` or `process.invariant.<name>` identifiers. Scope and force are represented by `FitnessSignalId`; weights, threshold, derivations and decisions remain unchanged.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: deterministic scoring, policy construction or bridge derivation creates a fitness signal
        then: the signal is constructed through `FitnessSignalId` and exposed as its canonical string form
        and:
          - no consumer infers force by inspecting a name prefix
          - existing score values and promotion decisions are unchanged
      - id: S2
        when: a mutation contract is rendered as canonical S-expression IR
        then: scope and name are rendered as nested atoms and gate/objective position carries the role
        and:
          - a name cannot move a signal between roles
          - names remain safe canonical atoms
      - id: S3
        when: MCP output serializes measured and invariant fitness signals
        then: measured objectives precede invariants and each group is sorted by canonical identifier
        and:
          - legacy unscoped and `hard_gate_*` keys are accepted on read and emitted canonically
          - output remains valid, bounded JSON

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: domain/FitnessSignalIdTest.acceptsLegacyKeysSoPersistedResultsCanBeReEmittedCanonically
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/MutationContractCanonicalizerTest.renderingPlacesRoleInThePositionNotTheName
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/EvolveMcpToolTest.legacyKeysAreReEmittedInCanonicalForm
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add the domain identifier type and legacy parsing compatibility
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: migrate deterministic scoring, policy and bridge identifiers without changing numeric behavior
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: render fitness signals structurally in the canonical S-expression IR
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: partition MCP output by typed force and normalize legacy keys at the output boundary
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: update README, glossary, knowledge, change records and handoff to describe the applied scheme and its remaining severity-class deferral
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - enforce the proposed integrity, safety, correctness and shape severity classes
  - add process-scoped signals to the live candidate scorer
  - change objective weights, promotion threshold or score derivation
  - migrate or rewrite historical ledger files in place

risks:
  - legacy result maps may contain identifiers outside the known old naming forms; those fail closed at the typed parsing boundary
